// The king's guard on the plateau.
=== start
[flag verc_north] -> gone
"The king sees whoever he wants to see." He looks you up and down. "You're armed. Keep it that way, and keep it in its sheath, and we'll be friends."
* "Who are you?" -> who
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== who
"I rode with him when he had twelve men and his uncle's dogs after him." He says it without boasting; it's a fact, like the weather. "Now he has the whole of Gaul. Most of it. He'll have the rest."
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== gone
"The king's gone north, into the Bituriges." He doesn't sound happy to be left behind. "Somebody has to hold the plateau. They say it's an honor."
* "Goodbye." -> END
